// uop_fn/uop_txt trap on any spelling ufn_name does not carry -- `find_str`
// answers -1 and the lookup indexes off the front of `names`. Nothing built
// by txt_setup has such a spelling (a type's own name is never an operator),
// so this builds two nodes whose `ns` is "/" and "%" -- ufn_name's own
// table, minus ">>" since one case each is enough to see two different
// unsigned builtins chosen.
uop_fixture() {
  int u = newleaf("prim", 4, 1, "/", "");
  int md = newleaf("prim", 4, 1, "%", "");
} return void;
given txt_fixture ():() then calls newleaf:("prim", 4, 1, "/", "")
given txt_fixture ():() then calls newleaf:("prim", 4, 1, "%", "")
